Sval: Remove Mozilla's AI features

Sval ships no AI feature (spec §2, principle 6). Smart Window, the
chatbot sidebar and its menus, link previews, page assist, smart tab
groups, the address bar's Smartbar and AI chat result, page data, the
page extractor, the multiline editor and the AI Controls settings pane go
whole, with their startup hooks, actors, strings, prefs, Nimbus features,
policies (AIControls, GenerativeAI), builtin theme and tests. The
on-device inference engine stays for Translations' EngineProcess, without
the vendored runtimes only those features loaded (ONNX Runtime,
Transformers.js, wllama, the OpenAI client) and their pipelines. The C++
allowlists in nsFrameLoader.cpp, nsContentSecurityUtils.cpp and
DOMSecurityMonitor.cpp still name the Smart Window documents.

